# Rust build artefacts (the workspace lives under impl/)
/impl/target/
**/target/
# The local CI script keeps a SEPARATE target dir per (checker x feature set) — clippy and rustc
# are different compilers to cargo's fingerprints, so sharing one rebuilds the workspace on every
# alternation. Those dirs are named `target-clippy`, `target-unaudited`, `target-check`, …, none of
# which the patterns above match — and a `git add impl` then stages twelve thousand build
# artefacts. Ignore the whole family, not each name.
**/target-*/

# Local run state (relay-id, demo profile directories)
/impl/.run/
.run/

# Agent tooling and private memory (personal data — never published)
/.claude/

# Raw project notes — never published
/mosaic_chat.txt

# Editors / OS
*.swp
*~
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
KARST_logo_kit.zip
/POSITIONING.md
1.zip
site/
site_gitignore/
KARST_logo_kit/
KARST_screenshots/
POS2_GITIGNORE.md

# Scratch analysis notes — the suffix IS the marker, so a new one is ignored by
# construction rather than by remembering to stage explicit paths.
*_gitignore*.md
*_gitignore*/
